==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sla-pro|ru}} {{m|sla-pro|*jьmę}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ru}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₁nómn̥}}. 

The so-called '''[[н]]'''-declension of this and nine other similar neuter nouns stems from the fact that the word-final '''-[[я]]''' was the nasal vowel [[Ѧ]], [[ѧ]] (little [[yus]]) in [[Old Church Slavonic]] and Late Proto-Slavic, resulting in the '''-ен-''' before all the case endings in the modern language. Compare the declension of Old Church Slavonic {{term|sc=Cyrl|имѧ|tr=imę|lang=cu}}.

